  "body": "When a language model generates text, it computes a probability distribution over its vocabulary using the softmax function. Applying top-k filtering drops all tokens outside the top $k$ highest-scoring choices, setting their probabilities to zero.\n\n[[visual:1]]\n\nTo ensure the remaining probabilities still sum to $1$, the model renormalizes the surviving values by dividing each by the sum of the kept probabilities. Look at the chart to see how the original probabilities scale up after filtering.\n\nThis renormalization changes the reported probability of every chosen token. If you log the model output, the recorded confidence reflects this post-filtering distribution rather than the raw softmax score.",
