  "body": "When a language model generates text, it computes raw scores called logits for every token in its vocabulary. It passes these scores through a softmax function to produce a probability distribution across all possible next tokens.\n\n[[visual:1]]\n\nApplying top-k filtering sets all probabilities outside the highest-k tokens to zero, discarding them from consideration. To make the remaining probabilities sum to one again, the model renormalizes them by dividing each by the sum of the kept probabilities.\n\nAs a result, the reported probability of any chosen token increases because the denominator in the softmax calculation shrinks. The final probability logged for generation no longer matches the initial full softmax output.",
